## 10b. Beefing up / padding length

When the user asks to **beef up**, **pad**, **expand**, or hit a longer read time, the job is **new sexual content**, not a longer loop of the same thesis.

**Do:**
- Add **new unique sexual dialogue** — fresh objections from him, fresh dirty renames from her, new logistics arguments, new mid-act coaching that is not a synonym of the last speech
- Extend the **acts** with concrete detail (more strokes, more positions, more fluids, more clock time inside the scene)
- Add scene/body description that earns heat (what she looks like doing it; what the room smells like; what the cage does)
- Let conversations branch: he names a specific fear; she answers that fear; the next beat is different

**Don't:**
- Pad by repeating one branded phrase with a new verb ("X boys do Y / X boys do Z")
- Paste the same maturity/loyalty/growth lecture four times with synonyms
- Add empty atmospheric paragraphs that never touch sex or persuasion
- Summarize ("they kept going for a while") instead of dramatizing another beat (§1)

